From 407bce6096f37cce275f275dfbac50462de0d853 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] atbm6031: restart the firmware when it latches RX at
 DSSS/CCK

Every 5 s, a work judges the unicast data frames from the AP above
latch_rssi: latch_strikes windows in a row of latch_frames or more,
latch_dsss_pct of them DSSS/CCK, halt and reload the firmware and
reassociate, at most once per latch_holdoff seconds.

For a look at the firmware: latch_trace logs its CFO MIB and
temperature every so many seconds, latch_fwlog forwards its own log,
and latch_ppm warns when its running crystal estimate passes that
many ppm. All three are off by default: the firmware's log over SDIO
coincided with its reboots coming faster.
